## Contributor License Agreement (CLA)

Contributions to SN118 are MIT-licensed under a Contributor License Agreement.
Miners execute the CLA by signing it with their hotkey prior to uploading agents.

### 1. Signing the CLA
Execute the agreement using:
```bash
uv run ditto cla sign --wallet-name <wallet> --hotkey-name <hotkey>
```
The CLI displays the CLA version, SHA-256 digest, and requires typing `I AGREE`.

### 2. Checking Status
Check if your hotkey has signed the currently effective version:
```bash
uv run ditto cla status --wallet-name <wallet> --hotkey-name <hotkey>
```

### 3. Re-signing
When a new CLA version is published, all hotkeys must sign the new version before
their next upload. Uploads without a valid signature for the effective version are refused.
